From: Douglas Teles <dga.teles@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 09:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: px30: GPU OPPs the clock really makes, 650 from npll

clk_gpu is gpll (1200MHz) through an integer divider or a half divider,
so the 560MHz OPP ran at 480MHz with 560's voltage, and the 650MHz OPP
at 600MHz. Measured on an R36S with the userspace governor:

  requested 560MHz -> clk_gpu 480MHz, vdd_logic 1.125V
  requested 650MHz -> clk_gpu 600MHz, vdd_logic 1.15V

The 560 step now says 480MHz, at the voltage it already ran at. npll
goes to 1300MHz (vopl, its only other user, is off on these boards) so
that patch 061 can make a real 650MHz = npll/2; that OPP keeps its
turbo-mode flag (archr-perf-limits leaves it to the player). The node
names stay, since the boot tuning overlay addresses steps by them.
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/px30.dtsi	2026-11-23 08:16:04.854833690 -0300
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/px30.dtsi	2026-11-23 08:46:34.151963353 -0300
@@ -1163,7 +1163,9 @@
 			<&cru HCLK_BUS_PRE>, <&cru HCLK_PERI_PRE>,
 			<&cru PCLK_BUS_PRE>, <&cru SCLK_GPU>;
 
-		assigned-clock-rates = <1188000000>,
+		/* npll: 1300MHz, the GPU's 650 (patch 061); vopl, its only
+		 * other user, is off on every RK3326 board. */
+		assigned-clock-rates = <1300000000>,
 			<200000000>, <200000000>,
 			<150000000>, <150000000>,
 			<100000000>, <200000000>;
@@ -1413,8 +1415,15 @@
 			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <400000000>;
 			opp-microvolt = <1100000>;
 		};
+		/*
+		 * clk_gpu comes from gpll (1200MHz) through an integer or a
+		 * half divider: 1200/n or 1200/(n+0.5). The stock 560MHz ran
+		 * at 480 (measured on an R36S), so this step says 480; 650
+		 * comes from npll at 1300MHz (patch 061). The node names stay:
+		 * archr-boot-tuning's overlay addresses the steps by them.
+		 */
 		opp-560000000 {
-			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <560000000>;
+			opp-hz = /bits/ 64 <480000000>;
 			opp-microvolt = <1125000>;
 		};
 		opp-600000000 {
